  "texts": {
    "preamble": "Kallu vs State Of U.P. on 30 September, 2019 Author: Siddharth Bench: Siddharth",
    "facts": "Submission is that the applicant made complaint against Sub-Inspector, Manoj Kumar posted at Transport Nagar, Meerut and it has been submitted that he has falsely implicated him in number of cases. Offence under sections 60 of Excise Act is bailable and trible by Magistrate. False recovery has been alleged. The applicant is languishing in jail since 10.07.2019, who is not a previous convict. On the other hand learned AGA has opposed the prayer for bail. Kallu vs State Of U.P. on 30 September, 2019 Indian Kanoon - http://indiankanoon.org/doc/88035728/ 1",
    "arguments": "Keeping in view the nature of the offence, evidence on record regarding complicity of the accused, submissions of the learned counsel for the parties noted herein above, larger mandate of the Article 21 of the Constitution of India and the dictum of Apex Court in the case of Dataram Singh Vs. State of U.P. and another reported in (2018)3 SCC 22",
